of all the places I've been and stories  I've covered for Sky News my trip to the  island of Tanna who was probably my  favorite it was Prince Philip's 90th  birthday and I wanted to celebrate with  the tribe who worship Him as a god the  strange tale of devotion to a Greek born  British royal has its roots in a local  legend of a volcano which gave birth to  a white man who married a queen the  local chief sent her traditional club to  Buckingham Palace as a gift and when the  Duke sent back a picture of him holding  it his status as a deity was confirmed  for my trip I brought with me some  Philips souvenirs and a biography which  rather contradicts the tribes beliefs  the people of Yunnan and village always  hoped their prince would come to visit  but the news of his withdraw from public  life ends that dream in 2011 they had to  make do with me performing the opening  ceremony for a new shrine perhaps  they'll invite me back again as a mortal  stand-in for the man they call a God in  woods  Sky News no longer in Vanuatu
 

